{"kind":"doc","route":"/guide/testing/architecture/dependency-cycles","title":"No dependency cycles","blocks":[{"t":"heading","level":1,"id":"no-dependency-cycles","children":[{"t":"text","text":"No dependency cycles"}]},{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"code","text":"assertNoDependencyCycles"},{"t":"text","text":" checks directed "},{"t":"code","text":"depends-on"},{"t":"text","text":" edges between services,"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"components and computeds:"}]},{"t":"code","lines":[{"tokens":[{"text":"export","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" "},{"text":"function","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" "},{"text":"keepTheDependencyGraphAcyclic","kind":"function"},{"text":"(","kind":"punctuation"},{"text":"graph"},{"text":":","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" "},{"text":"ArchitectureGraph","kind":"type"},{"text":") {","kind":"punctuation"}]},{"tokens":[{"text":"  "},{"text":"assertNoDependencyCycles","kind":"function"},{"text":"(graph.graph);","kind":"punctuation"}]},{"tokens":[{"text":"}","kind":"punctuation"}]}],"filename":"","language":"ts","numbered":false,"firstLine":1},{"t":"heading","level":2,"id":"what-it-prevents","children":[{"t":"text","text":"What it prevents"}]},{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"The obvious cycle is two services that construct each other:"}]},{"t":"code","lines":[{"tokens":[{"text":"Left → Right → Left"}]}],"filename":"","language":"","numbered":false,"firstLine":1},{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"In source, it often appears as a harmless pair of "},{"t":"code","text":"yield*"},{"t":"text","text":" calls. At runtime it"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"can fail as a recursive construction, an incomplete service or a provider that"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"only breaks when a route is first visited."}]},{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"The rule also catches a self-dependency and cycles involving computed values."}]},{"t":"heading","level":2,"id":"shared-dependencies-are-not-cycles","children":[{"t":"text","text":"Shared dependencies are not cycles"}]},{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"This is valid:"}]},{"t":"code","lines":[{"tokens":[{"text":"AdminPage  → Auth"}]},{"tokens":[{"text":"Checkout   → Auth"}]}],"filename":"","language":"","numbered":false,"firstLine":1},{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"Both branches depend on a shared kernel; there is no path back from "},{"t":"code","text":"Auth"},{"t":"text","text":" to"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"either branch. "},{"t":"code","text":"provides"},{"t":"text","text":", "},{"t":"code","text":"contains"},{"t":"text","text":", "},{"t":"code","text":"loads"},{"t":"text","text":" and "},{"t":"code","text":"renders"},{"t":"text","text":" are structural"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"edges and are not treated as dependency cycles."}]},{"t":"heading","level":2,"id":"how-to-break-a-real-cycle","children":[{"t":"text","text":"How to break a real cycle"}]},{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"Usually one side should depend on a smaller contract:"}]},{"t":"list","ordered":false,"items":[[{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"extract a read-only service from the two large services;"}]}],[{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"move shared policy into a third service;"}]}],[{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"pass a value as an input instead of resolving the owning service;"}]}],[{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"move a derived value into the consumer instead of publishing it back."}]}]]},{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"Do not silence a cycle by adding an "},{"t":"code","text":"allow"},{"t":"text","text":" list: this assertion has no such"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"escape hatch because a cycle changes construction semantics."}]},{"t":"heading","level":2,"id":"see-also","children":[{"t":"text","text":"See also"}]},{"t":"list","ordered":false,"items":[[{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"link","href":"/craft/guide/app/service-scopes","external":false,"children":[{"t":"text","text":"Service scopes"}]}]}],[{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"link","href":"/craft/learn/04-compose","external":false,"children":[{"t":"text","text":"Composing services"}]}]}]]}],"outline":[{"level":2,"id":"what-it-prevents","text":"What it prevents"},{"level":2,"id":"shared-dependencies-are-not-cycles","text":"Shared dependencies are not cycles"},{"level":2,"id":"how-to-break-a-real-cycle","text":"How to break a real cycle"},{"level":2,"id":"see-also","text":"See also"}]}